<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Melno</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1422">1422</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Melno, Peace of Lake Melno · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gollub-war">Gollub War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Melno was signed on 27 September 1422 near Lake Melno between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and the allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gollub-war">Gollub War</a>. The Order gave up its claims to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitia">Samogitia</a> permanently, and the treaty fixed the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, which remained essentially unchanged for about five centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-melno.jpg" alt="Treaty of Melno" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: S. Bollmann · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teutonic_Order_1410.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
